subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, RT = (M, θ, ξ) an integer multiplicity triple in U of dimension n+1 (IMRep U (n+1)), f : ℝ^P → ℝ L-Lipschitz (L ≥ 0), and g : ℝ^P → ℝ^P Borel. Write T_xM := approxTangentPlane (n+1) M x and M_t := M ∩ {g ≠ 0} ∩ f⁻¹(t). Assume:
(G1) |g(x)| ≤ L for all x;
(G2) g(x) ∈ T_xM for H^{n+1}-a.e. x ∈ M;
(G3) for every Borel φ : ℝ^P → [0, ∞], t ↦ ∫_{M_t} φ dHⁿ is a.e.-measurable on ℝ and ∫_ℝ ∫_{M_t} φ dHⁿ dt = ∫_M |g| φ dH^{n+1};
(G4a) every M_t is countably n-rectifiable;
(G4b) for every t with Hⁿ(M_t ∩ K) < ∞ for all compact K ⊆ U: for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ M_t, M_t has approximate tangent space T_xM ∩ g(x)^⊥ (= T_xM ⊓ (ℝ∙g(x))ᗮ) at x.
(Hᵏ = μHE[k].) Then there is a family (R_t)_{t∈ℝ} of integer multiplicity triples in U of dimension n (Rs : ℝ → IMRep U n), R_t = (M'_t, θ_t, ξ_t), such that:
(1) M'_t ⊆ f⁻¹(t) for every t;
(2) for every Borel W ⊆ ℝ^P, t ↦ μ_{R_t}(W) (= R_t.measure W) is a.e.-measurable and ∫_ℝ μ_{R_t}(W) dt ≤ L·μ_{RT}(W) (lower integral in [0, ∞]; μ_{RT} = RT.measure);
(3) for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U), s ↦ τ(R_s)(ω) := R_s.action ω is Lebesgue integrable on ℝ;
(4') for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U) and a < b: ∫_a^b τ(R_s)(ω) ds = ∫_{M∩{a<f<b}} θ·⟨g♭∧ω, ξ⟩ dH^{n+1}, where g♭∧ω := alternatizeUncurryFin((innerSL ℝ g(x)).smulRight ω(x)) and ⟨α, ζ⟩ = ζ(α) (Bochner integrals; the left side is the interval integral).

Assume (TL): for all P, n ∈ ℕ, every open U ⊆ ℝ^P and all Borel sets A ⊆ B ⊆ U with Hⁿ(B ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U (Hⁿ = μHE[n]), for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ A and every linear subspace Q of ℝ^P: B has approximate tangent space Q at x iff A has approximate tangent space Q at x (HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt, Simon Ch. 3, 1.4).
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, M ⊆ U Borel and countably (n+1)-rectifiable with H^{n+1}(M ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U, and f : ℝ^P → ℝ L-Lipschitz (L ≥ 0). Then there exist, for j ∈ ℕ, sets V_j, C_j, Y_j ⊆ ℝ^{n+1}, maps ψ_j : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P and F_j : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ, and a map g : ℝ^P → ℝ^P such that:
(a) V_j is open, ψ_j is C¹ on V_j and injective on V_j, Dψ_j(y) is injective for every y ∈ V_j, and ψ_j(V_j) ⊆ U;
(b) C_j is compact, C_j ⊆ V_j, Y_j is Borel, Y_j ⊆ C_j, and F_j is C¹ on ℝ^{n+1};
(c) ψ_j(Y_j) ⊆ M for every j, the sets ψ_j(Y_j) are pairwise disjoint, and H^{n+1}(M ∖ ⋃_j ψ_j(Y_j)) = 0;
(d) for every j and y ∈ Y_j: f(ψ_j(y)) = F_j(y), and M has approximate tangent space Dψ_j(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) at ψ_j(y) (dimension n+1);
(e) g is Borel, |g(x)| ≤ L for every x, g(x) = 0 whenever x ∉ ⋃_j ψ_j(Y_j), and for every j and y ∈ Y_j: g(ψ_j(y)) ∈ Dψ_j(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) and ⟨g(ψ_j(y)), Dψ_j(y)e⟩ = DF_j(y)e for every e ∈ ℝ^{n+1}.
(g is the tangential gradient ∇^M f of Simon Ch. 3, 2.1, on the pieces ψ_j(Y_j).)

Assume (TL): for all P, n ∈ ℕ, every open U ⊆ ℝ^P and all Borel sets A ⊆ B ⊆ U with Hⁿ(B ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U (Hⁿ = μHE[n]), for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ A and every linear subspace Q of ℝ^P: B has approximate tangent space Q at x iff A does (HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt, Simon Ch. 3, 1.4).
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, RT = (M, θ, ξ) an integer multiplicity triple in U of dimension n+1 (IMRep U (n+1)), and f : ℝ^P → ℝ L-Lipschitz (L ≥ 0). Write T_xM := approxTangentPlane (n+1) M x, γ_{a,b}(s) := min{1, max{0, (b − s)/(b − a)}}, and for g : ℝ^P → ℝ^P and t ∈ ℝ, M_t := M ∩ {g ≠ 0} ∩ f⁻¹(t). Then there is a Borel map g : ℝ^P → ℝ^P with:
(G1) |g(x)| ≤ L for every x;
(G2) g(x) ∈ T_xM for H^{n+1}-a.e. x ∈ M;
(G3) for every Borel φ : ℝ^P → [0, ∞], t ↦ ∫_{M_t} φ dHⁿ is a.e.-measurable on ℝ and ∫_ℝ ∫_{M_t} φ dHⁿ dt = ∫_M |g| φ dH^{n+1};
(G4a) M_t is countably n-rectifiable for every t;
(G4b) for every t such that Hⁿ(M_t ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U: for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ M_t, M_t has approximate tangent space T_xM ∩ g(x)^⊥ (= T_xM ⊓ (ℝ∙g(x))ᗮ) at x;
(G5) for all a < b, every sequence (h_k) of C¹ functions ℝ^P → ℝ with ‖Dh_k(x)‖ ≤ c (all k, x) converging uniformly on ℝ^P to γ_{a,b}∘f, and every Borel W : ℝ^P → ℝ^P with |W| ≤ c', W = 0 outside some compact K ⊆ U, and W(x) ∈ T_xM for H^{n+1}-a.e. x ∈ M:
 ∫_M θ(x) Dh_k(x)[W(x)] dH^{n+1}(x) → ∫_{M∩{a<f<b}} θ(x)·(−(b − a)⁻¹⟨g(x), W(x)⟩) dH^{n+1}(x) as k → ∞.
